UPDATE herbal.herbs
SET class_notes_synopsis = $$<strong>Reishi Mushroom</strong> is a <strong>spirit remedy</strong> - "invite the light back in; restores the sparkle in the eyes"; a power herb alongside <a href="?herb=43"><strong>Nettle</strong></a>, <a href="?herb=85"><strong>Plantain</strong></a>, <a href="?herb=1252"><strong>Solomon's Seal</strong></a>. Calming <strong>adaptogen</strong> especially for burnout and nervous exhaustion ("tired but wired"); sweet taste; gives more Qi or life force; use when burned out at moderate to higher doses over 3-6 months. For <strong>insomnia</strong> and nightmares long-term (shen disturbance in TCM); for <strong>depression</strong>; supports the <strong>heart</strong> - "standing strong in yourself"; for anxiety alongside <a href="?herb=2632"><strong>Lion's Mane Mushroom</strong></a>. <strong>Immune amphoteric</strong> - balancing: brings down immune excess, raises deficiency; for <strong>autoimmune conditions</strong>; immune modulating for <strong>thyroid</strong> health; immune adaptogen for <strong>psoriasis</strong> (reduce immune response in skin). Lowers <strong>cholesterol</strong>, protects against clot formation and platelet aggregation, <strong>hypotensive</strong>. Balances <strong>blood sugar</strong> and androgen hormones; reduces 5-alpha-reductase for hormone-related hair loss and elevated androgen in <strong>PMOS</strong>; alongside <a href="?herb=186"><strong>Saw Palmetto</strong></a>, <a href="?herb=1649"><strong>Nettle Root</strong></a>, <a href="?herb=203"><strong>Turmeric</strong></a>, <a href="?herb=14"><strong>Ginseng</strong></a> to down-regulate 5-alpha reductase. Pulmonary <strong>trophorestorative</strong> for chronic cough; lung tonic alongside <a href="?herb=61"><strong>Mullein</strong></a>, <a href="?herb=85"><strong>Plantain</strong></a>, <a href="?herb=9"><strong>Siberian Ginseng</strong></a>. Protects against oxidative stress; helps metabolize cortisol and endocrine-disrupting chemicals (BPA, triclosan); for <strong>adrenal and thyroid imbalance</strong>; for <strong>metabolic syndrome</strong> (elevated lipids, weight gain, ankle swelling, visceral fat). For <strong>autoimmune disease</strong> with ECM and fibromyalgia: in soups and wet foods; stay nourished. Hay fever terrain: prepare through winter with <a href="?herb=225"><strong>Astragalus</strong></a> and <a href="?herb=78"><strong>Licorice</strong></a> to lessen spring allergic responses and mineralize body. Chronic immune support for <strong>diarrhea</strong> alongside <a href="?herb=225"><strong>Astragalus</strong></a>. Adaptogen/immune tonic protocol with <a href="?herb=225"><strong>Astragalus</strong></a> and <a href="?herb=17"><strong>Schizandra</strong></a>. With <a href="?herb=2238"><strong>White Peony</strong></a> synergy. For <strong>long COVID</strong>: stealth viral infections causing chronic pain and achy body. For <strong>influenza</strong>: use after acute phase resolves. For <strong>hypertension in pregnancy</strong>: second choice; research supports beneficial effects; partially protective against oxidative stress; helps metabolize endocrine-disrupting chemicals; best used as food/soup form (not powders) during pregnancy. Alternative to <a href="?herb=225"><strong>Astragalus</strong></a> in damp or fungal conditions (Astragalus polysaccharides can aggravate damp/fungal). Pre-biotic fiber and immune modulation. Extraction: needs water - alcohol only loses constituent complexity; designed for soups.$$
WHERE id = 11;

UPDATE herbal.herbs
SET class_notes_synopsis = $$<strong>Rhodiola</strong> is a <strong>drying</strong>, <strong>astringent</strong> (chalky, dry taste - organoleptic indicator of its astringent quality), <strong>nervine stimulant</strong>, <strong>adaptogen</strong>, and <strong>cardioprotective</strong> herb; "energetic heart medicine" - reduces stress-induced <strong>arrhythmias</strong>, modulates stress, normalizes <strong>blood pressure</strong>. Improves <strong>stamina</strong> and hormones; supports adapting and change rather than providing extra energy. Good for <strong>elevation sickness</strong> and camping trips. Formula: Rhodiola, <a href="?herb=127"><strong>Cardamom</strong></a>, <a href="?herb=76"><strong>Fennel</strong></a> tincture at 5 drops, 3x/day. Clarity and calmness formula: <a href="?herb=134"><strong>Lemon Balm</strong></a> glycerite, <a href="?herb=2233"><strong>Hibiscus</strong></a>, <a href="?herb=73"><strong>Hawthorn</strong></a>, Rhodiola. Adaptogen for wet constitution alongside <a href="?herb=20"><strong>Ashwagandha</strong></a> (not if hot/wet) and <a href="?herb=17"><strong>Schizandra</strong></a>. Add a little glycerin to tincture to offset drying quality; + <a href="?herb=852"><strong>Shatavari</strong></a> to moisten. For <strong>common cold</strong>: immune tonic. <strong>Very drying - like Panax Ginseng and Tulsi, can overdo it if already depleted; supports adapting and change, not extra energy.</strong>$$
WHERE id = 16;

